  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>st</mi></mrow></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mo>&nbsp;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case, Carnot engine operates between temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>nd</mi></mrow></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mo>&nbsp;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case, as shown in the figure, a combination of two engines is used. The efficiency of this combination (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>nd</mi></mrow></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mo>&nbsp;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case) will be :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0072_d523f0f53451.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 217px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "same as the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>st</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "always greater than the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>st</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "always less than the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>st</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "may increase or decrease with respect to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>st</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> case",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The efficiency of a Carnot engine operating between two temperatures is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>For the first case : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>For the second case : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mrow><mi>net</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>200</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mrow><mi>net</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi></math>(first case)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#951;</mi></math>(second case)</p></blockquote>"
  }
